# Platform UX Review Gate — Cursor Enforcement

Before generating or modifying **any UI** (pages, components, forms, tables, modals, dashboards, profiles), validate against Nexora platform UX governance.

## Mandatory References (read when touching UI)

1. [Nexora Platform UX Constitution](../../docs/06-guidelines/NEXORA_PLATFORM_UX_CONSTITUTION.md) — supreme UX authority
2. [Platform UX Review Gate](../../docs/06-guidelines/PLATFORM_UX_REVIEW_GATE.md) — pre-merge checklist
3. [Platform Component Policy](../../docs/06-guidelines/PLATFORM_COMPONENT_POLICY.md) — frozen reusable components
4. [Inline Editing Standard](../../docs/06-guidelines/INLINE_EDITING_STANDARD.md)
5. [Edit Mode v2 Standard](../../docs/06-guidelines/EDIT_MODE_V2_STANDARD.md)
6. [ADR-021 Platform UX Constitution](../../docs/03-architecture/adr/ADR-021_PLATFORM_UX_CONSTITUTION.md)
7. [Easy Operator Forms Standard](../../docs/06-guidelines/EASY_OPERATOR_FORMS_STANDARD.md) — **standing Ahmed UX bar**

Also apply: [ERP Page Modal Pattern](erp-page-modal-patterns.mdc) · [No Native Date Inputs](no-native-date-inputs.mdc) · [Easy Operator Forms](easy-operator-forms.mdc)

## Pre-Implementation Checklist (UI work)

When creating or changing screens, confirm:

- [ ] **Navigation** — route in app navigation; correct permission; shell wrapper (`PageContainer`, `HrShell`, etc.)
- [ ] **Page type** — list-first for operational CRUD; modal create/edit (`?create=1`, `?edit=id`)
- [ ] **Components** — `EnterpriseDataTable`, `EntityLookup`, `DatePicker`, `RecordFormDialog`, `EditableField` from `@/shared/ui`
- [ ] **No native date** — never `<input type="date" />`
- [ ] **No raw UUIDs** — `EntityLookup` for all relations
- [ ] **Styled selects** — `Select` or `nativeSelectClassName` in dark mode
- [ ] **Permissions** — `requirePermission` in loaders/actions; lock icon when read-only
- [ ] **Cross-engine** — `ownership="cross-engine"` + workflow opener; no silent cross-domain mutation
- [ ] **States** — loading, empty, error, skeleton where appropriate
- [ ] **Tokens** — `hsl(var(--surface))`, `--border`, `--foreground`; visible buttons in dark mode
- [ ] **Easy operator forms** — `FieldGroup` labels; max 3 cols; create before filter; full i18n enums/statuses ([standard](../../docs/06-guidelines/EASY_OPERATOR_FORMS_STANDARD.md))
- [ ] **Audit / notifications** — on business-critical mutations per module pattern

## Forbidden Without Exception (ADR-021)

- Module-local table, form, date, or lookup implementations
- Full-page `/new` or `/edit` routes for simple master data (use list + modal)
- Read-only-only profile pages without inline edit path
- Direct Sonner/toast imports in apps (use `platform.feedback`)
- Placeholder-only form fields without persistent labels
- More than 3 columns for mixed operator create forms (`xl:grid-cols-4+`)
- English enum/status labels in localized UI
- Module-local labeled-field wrappers when `FieldGroup` exists
- Redesigning unrelated pages when task is scoped elsewhere

## When Shipping UI

1. Self-score against [Design Review Process](../../docs/06-guidelines/DESIGN_REVIEW_PROCESS.md) (target ≥ 85/100).
2. Note [UX Migration Tracker](../../docs/06-guidelines/UX_MIGRATION_TRACKER.md) row if module % changes.
3. Document Review Gate exceptions in PR — no silent bypass.

## Architecture Boundaries (unchanged by UX)

UX governance does **not** permit:

- Changing business logic or runtime ownership to "fix" UI
- Bypassing attendance, leave, payroll, or inventory engines
- Payroll calculation or localization changes under UX tasks

## Quick Component Map

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Labeled field | `FieldGroup` |
| List | `EnterpriseDataTable` |
| Relation field | `EntityLookup` |
| Date | `DatePicker` / `DatePickerField` |
| Create/edit modal | `RecordFormDialog` |
| Profile field | `EditableField` / `EditableSectionCard` |
| Dashboard metric | `KpiCard` / `DashboardTemplate` |
| Filters | `FilterBar`, `SearchBar` |
| Approval UI | `ApprovalCard` |

If a needed primitive is missing, propose platform extension — do not fork in `src/features/`.
